{"id":"word:hebrew:H5483","type":"word","title":"סוּס","subtitle":"H5483 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a horse (as leaping); also a swallow (from its rapid flight )","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to סוּס (H5483) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 141 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"סוּס (çûwç) means a horse (as leaping); also a swallow (from its rapid flight ) First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 5 6."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"סוּס","transliteration":"çûwç","pronunciation":"soos","strong":"H5483","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5483","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["סוּסִ֖ים","ס֣וּס","סוּסִ֥ים","וְ/ס֣וּס","סוּסִ֔ים"],"morphs":[["HNcmpa",34],["HNcmsa",18],["HTd/Ncmpa",15],["HC/Ncmsa",13],["HTd/Ncmsa",11],["HNcmpc/Sp3ms",7],["HRd/Ncmpa",6],["HRd/Ncmsa",5],["HNcmpc/Sp3mp",4],["HNcmsc",4]]},"definitions":{"short":"a horse (as leaping); also a swallow (from its rapid flight )","usage":"crane, horse (-back, -hoof). Compare 6571 .","full":"H5483. cuwc I. סוּס noun [masculine] swallow or swift ( cypselus , Tristr FFP 82 ff. ) ( סוּסָיָא ᵑ7 Isa 38:14 ); &#8212; as twittering 38:14 (in simile); ᵐ5 χελιδών , ᵑ9 pullus hirundinis ;; so Jer 8:7 Kt (Qr סִיס wrongly; perhaps to distinguish from following, so Gie), ᵐ5 id ., ᵑ9 hirundo . II. סוּס 138 noun masculine Exod 15:1 horse (Late Hebrew סוּסָה סוּס, Aramaic סוּסְיָא Mandean סוסיא , Sinaitic id ., Lzb 328 ; Assyrian sisû (sisû ?) Dl HWB 506 ; Tel Amarna su-u[su] Wkl TA.191, 24 ; probably foreign word compare Nö M 147 Erman Ägypten 649; English tr. 490 ); — ׳ס absolute 1Kin 20:20 +; construct Exod 15:19 +; plural סוּסִים Gen 47:17 +, סֻסִים 2Sam 15:1 ; construct סוּסֵי 2Kin 2:11 ; suffix סוּסַי 1Kin 22:4 ; 2Kin 3:7 . סוּסֶיךָ Micah 5:9 + 4t., סוּסָיו Isa 5:28 +, סוּסֵיכֶס Amos 4:10 , סוּסֵיהֶם Josh 11:6 +; &#8212; horse: 1 non-Israel; chariot-horses of Canaanites Judg 5:22 (compare 5:28 ; 4:3 , 13 ; ס ׳עִקְבֵי ; ׳ס collective, as often), Josh 11:4 , 6 , 9 (JE); horses as property of Egyptians Gen 47:17 ; Exod 9:3 (both J), compare Zech 14:15 ; merchandise of Tyre Ezek 27:14 ; chariot-horses of Egypt [compare Hom 11.ix.384 ], Exod 14:9 , 23 (Psalms), 15:1 , 21 (poem), 15:19 (Psalms; on all see Di), Deut 11:4 ; Isa 31:1 , 3 ; Jer 46:4 , 9 ; Ezek 17:15 ; of Aram 1Kin 20:1 11 t. Kings ( 20:20 ridden , for flight), Assyrians Isa 5:28 3 t., Chaldeans Jer 4:13 6 t.; other nations Nahum 3:2 ; Jer 50:42 5 t.; as ridden 1Kin 20:20 (see above), Jeremiah 8:23; Ezek 38:4 , 15 13 t. (late). 2 in Israel; chariot-horses of Absalom 2Sam 15:1 , especially of Solomon, and later, 1Kin 5:6 ; 5:8 ; 10:25 , 28 , 29 , and || Chronicles; 18:5 and .(as war-equipment) 22:4 ; 2Kin 3:7 ; 9:33 ; 10:2 ; Prov 21:31 ; אֵשׁ סוּסֵי 2Kin 2:11 (Elijah), compare 6:17 ; consecration to sun 23:11 (compare RS Semitic 275; 2nd ed. 293 ); sign of luxury and apostasy Amos 4:10 ; Hosea 1:7 ; 14:4 ; Isa 2:7 ; Micah 5:9 ; Zech 9:10 , compare Deut 17:6 , 16 , but see Zech 14:20 ; in vision 6:2 (twice in verse); 6:3 (twice in verse); 6:6 ; ridden 2Kin 9:18-19 , 18:23 = Isa 36:8 ; Amos 2:15 4 t. Isaiah Jeremiah; in vision Zech 1:8 (twice in verse); הַס ׳שַׁעַר Jer 31:40 ; Neh 3:28 , compare 2Kin 11:16 2Chr 23:15 ; belongings of returned exiles Ezra 2:56 = Neh 7:68 van d. H. (omitted by Masora Baer Ginsb q. v.); description of horse Job 39:19 ; in various simile and figurative Amos 6:12 ; Jer 5:8 ; 8:6 ; 12:5 ; Ezek 23:20 ; Isa 63:13 ; Joel 2:4 ; Prov 27:3 ; Psa 32:9 ; 147:10 . 3 chariot-horses of ׳י Hab 3:15 (figurative of clouds), compare Zech 10:3 . &#8212; compare also סוּסִים חֲצַר , and רֶכֶשׁ מָּרָשׁ, .","rootNote":"or סֻס ; from an unused root meaning to skip (properly, for joy);","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 5 6","keyReferences":["1Kgs 5 6","1Kgs 5 8","1Kgs 10 25","1Kgs 10 28","1Kgs 10 29","1Kgs 18 5","1Kgs